"""Semantic extraction layer for the Azazael graph — authored by the LLM (Codebuff).

This is the Part-B semantic pass the graphify extraction spec describes. There is no
GEMINI/GOOGLE key on this host, so the agent IS the LLM. Every node here comes from
reading the doc corpus (288 project docs; the 1,238 `skills/` + `skills.win-backup/`
files are generated mirrors and are excluded from meaning extraction).

Design constraints that matter:
- IDs follow the spec format `{full_repo_relative_path_stem}_{entity}`, lowercased,
  non-alphanumerics to `_`. Never append chunk suffixes.
- `file_type` is one of the 3 valid non-code values: document | rationale | concept.
- Semantic nodes are ANCHORED to real AST node ids (resolved from labels) so this pass
  CONNECTS to the code graph instead of becoming another stranded island. That is the
  whole point of the exercise: 3,014 of 3,021 docs had no graph node at all.
- confidence_score is drawn from the spec's discrete set (1.0 / 0.95 / 0.85 / 0.75 /
  0.65 / 0.55); AMBIGUOUS uses 0.1-0.3. Never 0.5.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

